{"raw": {"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=523797736_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Head Coach Flag Football", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nAbout the Role: The Head Coach Flag Football position is a leadership role responsible for developing and managing a competitive and educational flag football program within an educational setting. The primary goal is to cultivate athletes' skills, teamwork, and sportsmanship while promoting physical fitness and a positive sporting environment. This role involves designing training sessions, strategizing game plans, and mentoring players to achieve both individual and team success. The Head Coach will also collaborate with school administrators, parents, and other coaches to ensure the program aligns with educational values and community standards. Ultimately, the position aims to foster a lifelong appreciation for sports and healthy competition among participants. Minimum Qualifications: Proven experience coaching flag football or a related sport at the youth or educational level. Strong knowledge of flag football rules, techniques, and strategies. Ability to communicate effectively with students, parents, and school staff. Background in physical education, sports management, or a related field is preferred. Certification in first aid and CPR or willingness to obtain upon hiring. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience as a head coach or assistant coach in an educational or community sports program. Formal coaching certification from a recognized sports organization. Experience working with diverse student populations and fostering inclusive team environments. Knowledge of athlete development principles and injury prevention techniques. Demonstrated ability to organize and manage sports events or tournaments. Responsibilities: Plan, organize, and conduct regular flag football practices and training sessions tailored to various skill levels. Develop game strategies, analyze team performance, and make real-time decisions during competitions. Mentor and motivate student-athletes to improve their skills, teamwork, and sportsmanship. Coordinate with school officials, parents, and other stakeholders to support program goals and logistics. Ensure compliance with safety protocols, league rules, and educational policies related to student athletics. Skills: The Head Coach will utilize strong leadership and communication skills daily to inspire and guide athletes toward their full potential. Strategic thinking and analytical skills are essential for developing effective game plans and adapting tactics during competitions. Organizational skills are critical for managing practice schedules, coordinating with stakeholders, and ensuring compliance with safety and educational standards. The ability to teach and mentor young athletes fosters skill development and positive team dynamics. Additionally, interpersonal skills help build trust and collaboration among players, parents, and school personnel, creating a supportive and motivating environment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=498131519_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Public Safety Officer Part-Time", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-19\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nThomas More University is seeking dedicated Part-time Public Safety Officers to join our team and make a meaningful difference in the lives of our students and campus community. \u00a0Public Safety Officers serve as ambassadors of safety and hospitality by providing visible patrols, responding to emergencies, assisting community members, and helping create an environment where learning, faith, and service can flourish. If you are committed to serving others with professionalism, integrity, and respect, we encourage you to apply. About Us : Thomas More is an academic community in Northern Kentucky that provides a Catholic liberal arts education to men and women who are seeking to live lives of meaning.\u00a0 As a Catholic diocsean university, Thomas More is university of the Diocese of Covington and as such is committed to the principles and beliefs that lay at the heart of Christianity, specifically those handed down by the Roman Catholic tradition. The university welcomes students and faculty of all faiths who have a desire to seek the Truth, do the Good, and love the Beautiful. Inspired by our three founding religious orders: the Benedictine Sisters, the Congregation of Divine Providence, and the Sisters of Notre Dame, our communal and academic life continues to faithfully follow the Catholic Intellectual Tradition.\u00a0 As a university founded through three religious orders,\u00a0 Thomas More University inherits a \u00a0 treasured history from those charisms. Inspired by our founding orders, the university is guided by our Characteristics of a Saint : Hospitality, Humility, Service, and Stewardship . We strive to support a welcoming community that recognizes the dignity of every person, approaches learning and relationships with openness and humility, serves others with compassion and purpose, and faithfully stewards the gifts, opportunities, and responsibilities entrusted to us. These values shape our culture, inform our decisions, and inspire our commitment to educating our students to live lives of meaning in service of the common good.\u00a0 As a liberal arts university, Thomas More University is committed to providing a liberal arts core of studies in the arts and sciences that is entirely informed by our engagement with the Catholic Intellectual Tradition. Devoted to the unity of faith and reason and the understanding that truth is one, the core seeks the integration of all disciplines. This integrative formation enables students to develop their capacity to discern the Truth, think critically, and engage in a sincere dialogue. The liberal arts foundation guides the career and professional paths students will take in the liberal arts, sciences, and business. Our students are invited to engage in a lifelog search for wisdom, not just information. Why Thomas More University? Commitment to Mission and Values : Thomas More University is guided by a mission that integrates faith and reason. Employees have the opportunity to contribute to a meaningful mission that emphasizes the holistic development of students in an inclusive, values-driven environment.\u00a0 Supportive Community : Working on campus at Thomas More University means being part of a close-knit community that encourages collaboration, respect, and integrity. The university promotes a culture of support and professional growth.\u00a0 Educational Benefits : Thomas More University offers tuition remission and other educational benefits for employees and their dependents, encouraging lifelong learning and development.\u00a0 Competitive Benefits Package : Employees are offered a comprehensive benefits package, including health, dental, and retirement benefits. What You Will Do: Respond to service calls, including unlocking buildings, providing escorts, assisting motorists, and responding to suspicious activity or emergencies. Patrol the campus by vehicle, golf cart, or foot to ensure full coverage of campus buildings and grounds. Identify and report maintenance concerns and campus hazards to appropriate staff. Provide security at university functions and athletic events as needed. Administer basic first aid, CPR, and AED, coordinating with medical responders when necessary. Assist students in crisis, working with university staff and external resources to ensure proper care. Respond to campus security and fire alarms, ensuring appropriate action is taken. Maintain clear, timely daily logs and incident reports. Promote shared responsibility for campus safety and enforce university policies with tact and diplomacy. Perform duties in line with university policies, including the TMU Employee Manual. Work flexible hours to ensure 24/7 safety coverage. Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent required; additional education in criminal justice or related fields welcome. Excellent customer service, interpersonal, and communication skills, with the ability to handle stressful situations and diverse personalities. Knowledge of campus safety and security procedures, including fire/life safety and access control systems. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with proficiency in English grammar, spelling, and report writing. Ability to interpret and enforce university regulations with firmness and diplomacy. Good judgment, discretion, and the ability to analyze situations accurately and adopt effective courses of action. Ability to work independently, confidentially, and with minimal supervision. Proficiency in or ability to quickly learn new technologies relevant to safety systems and campus operations. Working Hours : \u00a0Public Safety provides 24/7 coverage. Shifts may vary based on operational needs, and the officer\u2019s schedule will be determined by the Supervisor. \u00a0Physical Requirements:\u00a0 Frequently: interact and communicate with university members and others. Frequently: extended periods of sitting, standing, walking, and operating a golf cart or motor vehicle. As necessary: climb stairs and run. Regularly: sit for desk-based tasks, perform fine manipulation, use a telephone/radio, write by hand, and sort/file paperwork. Regularly: kneel/crawl, twist, and lift/carry/push/pull objects weighing up to 35 pounds.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=498598418_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Public Safety Officer", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-19\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nJob Posting Title Public Safety Officer Job Description Thomas More University is seeking dedicated full-time Public Safety Officers to join our team and make a meaningful difference in the lives of our students and campus community. \u00a0Public Safety Officers serve as ambassadors of safety and hospitality by providing visible patrols, responding to emergencies, assisting community members, and helping create an environment where learning, faith, and service can flourish. If you are committed to serving others with professionalism, integrity, and respect, we encourage you to apply. About Us : Thomas More is an academic community in Northern Kentucky that provides a Catholic liberal arts education to men and women who are seeking to live lives of meaning.\u00a0 As a Catholic diocsean university, Thomas More is university of the Diocese of Covington and as such is committed to the principles and beliefs that lay at the heart of Christianity, specifically those handed down by the Roman Catholic tradition. The university welcomes students and faculty of all faiths who have a desire to seek the Truth, do the Good, and love the Beautiful. Inspired by our three founding religious orders: the Benedictine Sisters, the Congregation of Divine Providence, and the Sisters of Notre Dame, our communal and academic life continues to faithfully follow the Catholic Intellectual Tradition.\u00a0 As a university founded through three religious orders,\u00a0 Thomas More University inherits a \u00a0 treasured history from those charisms. Inspired by our founding orders, the university is guided by our Characteristics of a Saint : Hospitality, Humility, Service, and Stewardship . We strive to support a welcoming community that recognizes the dignity of every person, approaches learning and relationships with openness and humility, serves others with compassion and purpose, and faithfully stewards the gifts, opportunities, and responsibilities entrusted to us. These values shape our culture, inform our decisions, and inspire our commitment to educating our students to live lives of meaning in service of the common good.\u00a0 As a liberal arts university, Thomas More University is committed to providing a liberal arts core of studies in the arts and sciences that is entirely informed by our engagement with the Catholic Intellectual Tradition. Devoted to the unity of faith and reason and the understanding that truth is one, the core seeks the integration of all disciplines. This integrative formation enables students to develop their capacity to discern the Truth, think critically, and engage in a sincere dialogue. The liberal arts foundation guides the career and professional paths students will take in the liberal arts, sciences, and business. Our students are invited to engage in a lifelog search for wisdom, not just information. Why Thomas More University? Commitment to Mission and Values : Thomas More University is guided by a mission that integrates faith and reason. Employees have the opportunity to contribute to a meaningful mission that emphasizes the holistic development of students in an inclusive, values-driven environment.\u00a0 Supportive Community : Working on campus at Thomas More University means being part of a close-knit community that encourages collaboration, respect, and integrity. The university promotes a culture of support and professional growth.\u00a0 Educational Benefits : Thomas More University offers tuition remission and other educational benefits for employees and their dependents, encouraging lifelong learning and development.\u00a0 Competitive Benefits Package : Full-time employees are offered a comprehensive benefits package, including health, dental, and retirement benefits. What You Will Do: Respond to service calls, including unlocking buildings, providing escorts, assisting motorists, and responding to suspicious activity or emergencies. Patrol the campus by vehicle, golf cart, or foot to ensure full coverage of campus buildings and grounds. Identify and report maintenance concerns and campus hazards to appropriate staff. Provide security at university functions and athletic events as needed. Administer basic first aid, CPR, and AED, coordinating with medical responders when necessary. Assist students in crisis, working with university staff and external resources to ensure proper care. Respond to campus security and fire alarms, ensuring appropriate action is taken. Maintain clear, timely daily logs and incident reports. Promote shared responsibility for campus safety and enforce university policies with tact and diplomacy. Perform duties in line with university policies, including the TMU Employee Manual. Work flexible hours to ensure 24/7 safety coverage. Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent required; additional education in criminal justice or related fields welcome. Excellent customer service, interpersonal, and communication skills, with the ability to handle stressful situations and diverse personalities. Knowledge of campus safety and security procedures, including fire/life safety and access control systems. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with proficiency in English grammar, spelling, and report writing. Ability to interpret and enforce university regulations with firmness and diplomacy. Good judgment, discretion, and the ability to analyze situations accurately and adopt effective courses of action. Ability to work independently, confidentially, and with minimal supervision. Proficiency in or ability to quickly learn new technologies relevant to safety systems and campus operations. Working Hours : \u00a0Public Safety provides 24/7 coverage. Shifts may vary based on operational needs, and the officer\u2019s schedule will be determined by the Supervisor. \u00a0Physical Requirements:\u00a0 Frequently: interact and communicate with university members and others. Frequently: extended periods of sitting, standing, walking, and operating a golf cart or motor vehicle. As necessary: climb stairs and run. Regularly: sit for desk-based tasks, perform fine manipulation, use a telephone/radio, write by hand, and sort/file paperwork. Regularly: kneel/crawl, twist, and lift/carry/push/pull objects weighing up to 35 pounds.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=472143068_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Director, Zembrodt Center for Entrepreneurship & Innovation", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-27\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nDirector Zembrodt Center for Entrepreneurship & Innovation (ZCEI) Division of Strategic Growth\u00a0 Thomas More University \u00a0 Position Summary Thomas More University invites applications for the position of Director of the Zembrodt Center for Entrepreneurship & Innovation (ZCEI). This is a full-time faculty appointment within the Robert W. Plaster College of Business that combines excellence in teaching with leadership of the University's entrepreneurship and innovation initiatives. The ZCEI Director serves as the chief academic and strategic leader of the ZCEI, advancing the University's mission by fostering an entrepreneurial mindset among students, cultivating partnerships throughout the regional business community, and expanding the University's reputation as the innovation destination for the Greater Cincinnati and Northern Kentucky region. The successful candidate will teach a standard four-course teaching load each semester and receive a two-course release per semester in recognition of the administrative responsibilities associated with directing the Center. Primary Responsibilities Academic Leadership Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in entrepreneurship, innovation, and related business disciplines. Develop and enhance an innovative entrepreneurship curriculum. Mentor students pursuing entrepreneurial ventures. Collaborate with faculty across disciplines. Center Leadership and Strategic Growth Provide strategic leadership for the ZCEI. Serve as the University's primary spokesperson for entrepreneurship and innovation. Position the University as a regional leader in entrepreneurship and innovation. Advancement and Philanthropy Partner with the Thomas More University Foundation and Institutional Advancement to cultivate donors and secure financial support. Engage in the procurement of grants to support the ZCEI, the College of Business, or related University areas when appropriate. Recruit, support, and engage with an external advisory board of key stakeholders in the entrepreneurial ecosystem of the region and/or proven entrepreneurs who might serve as potential investors in start ups who are engaged in formal relationships with the ZCEI. Entrepreneurial Venture Development Recruit and support promising startup companies. Provide mentorship and coaching in collaboration with the Advisory Board. Develop partnership agreements through revenue sharing, royalties, equity participation, or other mission-aligned investment models, as appropriate. \u00a0 Regional Partnership Development Build relationships with investors, venture capital firms, chambers of commerce, economic development organizations, and entrepreneurial partners. Design and facilitate workshops, executive education, speaker series, and professional development University Leadership Serve on the University's Strategic Growth Committee and contribute to strategic initiatives. Required Qualifications A master\u2019s degree in Entrepreneurship, Business Administration, Management, Innovation, or related discipline. Demonstrated success teaching entrepreneurship or related business disciplines. Experience leading entrepreneurship, innovation, incubation, or ecosystem initiatives. Excellent communication and collaboration skills. Preferred Qualifications A doctorate degree in a related field. Experience directing a university entrepreneurship center. Experience mentoring startups. Experience with fundraising, grants, or corporate partnerships. Personal Characteristics The successful candidate will be a visionary and collaborative leader who serves as a public ambassador for the Center and consistently demonstrates the Thomas More University core values of Hospitality, Humility, Service, and Stewardship. \u00a0 About the Center Mission The Dr. Anthony \u201965 and Geraldine \u201966 Zembrodt Center for Entrepreneurship and Innovation will equip students from diverse disciplines with essential, real-world skills that empower them to succeed in any field they pursue. We help students identify opportunities for innovation, starting a business, and learn how to approach the world with a creative, resourceful, and entrepreneurial mindset. Vision To be the leading destination for innovation in the region and a hub for our students and community to develop and foster entrepreneurial thinking to start and grow businesses and as a way of life", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=523463631_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Intl Student Services Coordinator / Designated School Official", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nInternational Student Services Coordinator / Designated School Official (DSO) Join Thomas More University in Welcoming the World Thomas More University is seeking an\u00a0 International Student Services Coordinator / Designated School Official (DSO) to serve as a trusted resource for our international students and a key partner in the University\u2019s commitment to student success, global education, and hospitality. This position provides leadership for international student services and F-1 immigration compliance while supporting students from admission through graduation. The Coordinator serves as the University\u2019s primary operational resource for\u00a0 F-1 regulations, SEVIS, SEVP requirements, and international student advising , while also helping create a welcoming and engaging campus experience. What You\u2019ll Do Serve as a Designated School Official (DSO) and institutional resource for F-1 immigration regulations and SEVP compliance. Maintain accurate SEVIS records, Forms I-20, Form I-17 requirements, and required federal reporting and deadlines. Advise international students on maintaining F-1 status, enrollment, employment authorization, travel, academic changes, CPT, OPT, transfers, and program extensions. Monitor international student status and provide proactive outreach when academic, compliance, or personal concerns arise. Coordinate international student orientation and programs supporting cultural adjustment, engagement, retention, and student success. Support Graduate & Global Education programs, including residency weekends and related student and faculty coordination. Collaborate with Enrollment, Academic Affairs, Student Life, Athletics, Financial Aid, the Registrar, faculty, advisors, and other campus partners. Maintain Terra Dotta and other systems supporting international student services. Monitor changes in federal regulations and communicate their impact to University leadership and campus partners. Contribute to departmental projects, strategic initiatives, international partnerships, and operational improvements. What We\u2019re Looking For Required Bachelor\u2019s degree. Ability to become and maintain eligibility as a Designated School Official. Excellent organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Strong attention to detail and ability to manage confidential information. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively across departments. Preferred Experience with SEVIS and F-1 immigration regulations. Experience in higher education, international education, student services, advising, enrollment, or a related field. Experience with Terra Dotta or comparable international student management systems. Experience advising international students or coordinating student programs and events. A Thomas More Saint At Thomas More University, we believe how we serve matters as much as what we accomplish. The successful candidate will demonstrate the Characteristics of a Saint through: Service \u2014 Respecting and advancing the Catholic mission and identity of Thomas More University. Stewardship \u2014 Responsibly managing student records, institutional resources, regulatory requirements, and the trust placed in this role. Humility \u2014 Approaching students and colleagues with openness, respect, a willingness to listen, and a commitment to serving others. Hospitality \u2014 Creating a welcoming environment where students from around the world feel known, supported, valued, and at home. Why This Role Matters International students bring unique perspectives, cultures, and experiences that enrich the entire Thomas More community. In this role, you will help ensure that international students have both the compliance guidance and personal support they need to thrive.. If you are organized, relationship-oriented, globally minded, and passionate about helping students succeed, we invite you to join the Thomas More University community. This position requires occasional evening and weekend work, including participation in Global Education residency weekends approximately three times per year.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=620221686_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Collection and Library Services Librarian", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nThomas More University is guided by the Characteristics of a Saint : Hospitality, Humility, Service, and Stewardship . We strive to support a welcoming community that recognizes the dignity of every person, approaches learning and relationships with openness and humility, serves others with compassion and purpose, and faithfully stewards the gifts, opportunities, and responsibilities entrusted to us. These values shape our culture, inform our decisions, and inspire our commitment to educating individuals who lead lives of purpose, integrity, and service. The Collections & Library Services Librarian serves as the operational and infrastructure backbone of the Benedictine Library, ensuring that resources are accessible, systems function effectively, and collections support the curricular and institutional needs of the University. This position provides leadership in access services, collections management, library systems, and resource workflows, while also contributing targeted liaison work and outreach connected to collections and services within a collaborative, small-library environment. Principle Duties & Responsibilities:\u00a0 \u00a0 1. Access Services & Resource Delivery Manage interlibrary loan (ILL) services Coordinate circulation, reserves, and resource delivery workflows Develop and maintain policies and procedures for access and service delivery Ensure consistent, reliable access to library resources \u00a0 2. Collections & Resource Management Implement collection development decisions in collaboration with library director, R&I librarian, and faculty Manage acquisitions, subscriptions, and vendor relationships Lead collection maintenance initiatives, including weeding and evaluation Support alignment of collections with curriculum and institutional priorities \u00a0 3. Cataloging, Processing & Discoverability Ensure timely processing and availability of library materials Perform or oversee copy cataloging and metadata maintenance Maintain organization and discoverability of physical and electronic resources \u00a0 4. Library Systems & Technology Administer and maintain the integrated library system (e.g., Koha) Troubleshoot access and resource issues Maintain the functional and service aspects of the library website, utilizing the LibGuides Content Management System (CMS) platform \u00a0 5. Government Documents (this is an electronic collection) Manage the government documents collection Ensure organization, accessibility, and compliance with applicable standards \u00a0 6. Records Management & Archives Support Coordinate records intake, organization, and storage Maintain selected archival materials at a basic operational level Support institutional records retention and preservation practices \u00a0 7. Outreach & Liaison (Targeted) Serve as liaison to assigned programs or departments (limited scope) Conduct outreach that promotes collections and services Support student engagement with library resources \u00a0 8. Assessment & Continuous Improvement (Shared) Contribute to assessment of library services and collections Collect and analyze data to inform decision-making Support institutional reporting and accreditation processes \u00a0 Additional Responsibilities Participate in campus committees and collaborative initiatives Engage in professional development and remain current with library trends and practices Perform other duties as assigned based on library priorities Education, Specialized and/or Technical Knowledge Requirements:\u00a0 \u00a0 Master of Library Science (MLS) from an ALA-accredited program preferred Experience in academic libraries or related settings preferred Familiarity with library systems, collections, or access services desirable \u00a0 Interested candidates please upload a resume and cover letter when completing the electronic application.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=620074517_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Head Coach Volleyball", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nThomas More University is guided by the Characteristics of a Saint : Hospitality, Humility, Service, and Stewardship . We strive to support a welcoming community that recognizes the dignity of every person, approaches learning and relationships with openness and humility, serves others with compassion and purpose, and faithfully stewards the gifts, opportunities, and responsibilities entrusted to us. These values shape our culture, inform our decisions, and inspire our commitment to educating individuals who lead lives of purpose, integrity, and service. Basic Purpose The Volleyball Coach for the Volleyball Program is responsible for management of all facets of the volleyball program including, but not limited to coaching/teaching, recruiting, budget management, administration,\u00a0 scheduling of competitions, team travel, weekly practice sessions, hiring and supervision of assistant coaches/interns, community service, student development, and compliance with NCAA, Great Midwest conference and university rules and regulations. Principle Duties & Activities \u2022 Develop a program of athlete recruitment commensurate with the aims and goals of Thomas More \u00a0University and appropriate for a member of the NCAA, Division II. \u2022 Plan and coordinate practice and game plans for intercollegiate competition. \u2022 Determine policies and procedures for team selection and athlete participation. \u2022 Make recommendations about game schedules and budget for the team. \u2022 Track the academic progress of the volleyball student-athletes and provide appropriate advice and assistance to help insure the successful completion of each players stated program of study. \u2022 Develop and implement a comprehensive fundraising program to raise funds necessary to offset expenses associated for non-budgeted expenses and spring training trips.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=605603259_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Assistant Professor of Marketing", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nAbout the Role: The Adjunct Assistant Professor of Marketing plays a pivotal role in delivering high-quality marketing education to undergraduate and/or graduate students within an academic institution. This position is responsible for designing and delivering engaging course content that reflects current marketing theories, practices, and trends, thereby preparing students for successful careers in the marketing field. The role involves fostering a dynamic and inclusive learning environment that encourages critical thinking, creativity, and practical application of marketing concepts. Additionally, the professor will contribute to curriculum development and collaborate with faculty members to enhance the overall academic program. Ultimately, this position aims to inspire and equip students with the knowledge and skills necessary to excel in the evolving marketing landscape while supporting the institution\u2019s mission of academic excellence and student success. Minimum Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in Marketing, Business Administration, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Demonstrated expertise in marketing principles and practices through academic or professional experience. Prior teaching experience at the college or university level is preferred but not mandatory. Strong communication and interpersonal skills to effectively engage with diverse student populations. Eligibility to work in the United States. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree (Ph.D. or DBA) in Marketing or a related discipline. Experience with online or hybrid course delivery platforms and instructional technologies. Professional marketing experience in industry sectors such as digital marketing, brand management, or market research. Record of scholarly activity or contributions to marketing research and publications. Experience mentoring students and supporting their professional development. Responsibilities: Develop and deliver course materials for marketing classes, including lectures, assignments, and assessments. Engage students through interactive teaching methods and provide timely feedback to support their academic growth. Stay current with marketing industry trends and integrate relevant real-world examples into the curriculum. Participate in departmental meetings and contribute to curriculum review and development processes. Maintain regular office hours to advise and mentor students on academic and career-related matters. Skills: The required and preferred skills are utilized daily to create an effective and engaging learning environment. Strong communication skills enable clear explanation of complex marketing concepts and foster meaningful interactions with students. Expertise in marketing theory and practice allows the professor to design relevant coursework that bridges academic knowledge with real-world application. Familiarity with instructional technologies supports the delivery of content in various formats, including in-person and online settings. Additionally, interpersonal and mentoring skills are essential for guiding students\u2019 academic progress and career aspirations, ensuring they receive comprehensive support throughout their educational journey.", "department": ""}}, "rows": {"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=523797736_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 488, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=523797736_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Head Coach Flag Football", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-08-24", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/defau